1
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:04,795
Let me know if you need anything else.

2
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:11,437
Finally, I can smoke.

3
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:14,696
It's not easy to find places
that allow it these days.

4
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:16,232
Being a smoker is tough.

5
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:22,437
But the good news, Imoko's school
trip to Kyoto starts today.

6
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:25,517
So now I can smoke at home as
much as I want and I love it!

7
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,617
Excuse me, ma 'am.

8
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,500
Apologies, but I'm afraid this
cafe only allows e-cigarettes.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,740
Ma 'am, are you all right?

10
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:25,100
Tepelo, te na me ta.

11
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:27,270
Hippiakusei.

12
00:01:31,460 --> 00:01:32,980
Odupini, steekurete.

13
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:43,550
Wala ta, la.

14
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:44,970
Just so.

15
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:50,177
Ganbaré, ganbaré, ganbaré yo, Lela.

16
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:54,320
If it's over, if it's
over, it's only a gold.

17
00:01:56,340 --> 00:02:01,540
If it's over, it's only a gold.

18
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:03,370
But...

19
00:02:03,453 --> 00:02:04,360
3401!

20
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:05,990
3401!

21
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:08,260
3401! 3401! 0101!

22
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,230
Yay!

23
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,170
Finally!

24
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:13,900
We're in Kyoto!

25
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:15,570
Look at it.

26
00:02:15,653 --> 00:02:16,483
It's amazing.

27
00:02:16,566 --> 00:02:17,396
There's so much gold.

28
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:18,817
Imoko. Huh?

29
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:21,177
You remember we're in high school, right?

30
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:23,977
Yeah, it's a little weird to
be this excited over a temple.

31
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:24,890
What do you mean?

32
00:02:24,973 --> 00:02:26,517
Don't you see? All the...

33
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:27,800
all of the gold.

34
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:28,957
We get it.

35
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,275
You're a fan of gold.

36
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:31,897
Can I say something?

37
00:02:31,980 --> 00:02:35,568
I know this place is famous,
but I do have a few suggestions.

38
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:39,877
First, I'd move all the
temples into the same area.

39
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:40,790
Hold on.

40
00:02:40,873 --> 00:02:43,957
Make it less like, you know, that
tourist trap of a clock tower up north.

41
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:46,977
Then people won't feel so disappointed
when they show up and see just this.

42
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:49,720
I can't believe what
I'm hearing! Well, okay.

43
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:52,417
I can think of some things
I'd like to see, too.

44
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,217
Hmm, yeah, I think that could work.

45
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:57,888
We could use Nintendo's overseas
profits to fund big parades.

46
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:02,417
And build a VR facility where guests
can play, like, VR Samurai Raid, right?

47
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,735
Now hold on a minute!

48
00:03:04,620 --> 00:03:07,738
Kyoto remains the heart and
soul of Japanese culture.

49
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:11,548
To twist it to fit modern
sensibilities devalues our history.

50
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:17,021
If twisting it for modern sensibilities
devalues our history, Then,

51
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:18,691
what's with the cat ears?

52
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:24,677
Apparently, Ashitaka Yoshimitsu
had a huge beast folk fetish.

53
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:27,137
I'm thinking the only twisted
thing here was his kink.

54
00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:28,514
It's giving Las Vegas.

55
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,461
Something wrong?

56
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:36,517
I didn't know there were so
many smoking areas in Kyoto.

57
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:39,677
This place does get millions of
visitors from all over the world.

58
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:43,337
The sign says you'll get fined a thousand
bucks if you smoke on the street.

59
00:03:43,420 --> 00:03:46,337
I guess it's better than
smoking around everyone else.

60
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:48,157
Did that make you think of your sister?

61
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:49,070
What?

62
00:03:49,153 --> 00:03:51,000
Well, uh...

63
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:54,851
Now I've suddenly started getting worried.

64
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:57,293
What if Yoni hurts herself or gets sick?

65
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:59,217
There's nothing that I could do from here.

66
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:01,597
And I don't think Mom
would be much of a help.

67
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:02,510
Imoko.

68
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:03,570
Yeah?

69
00:04:03,653 --> 00:04:05,437
Trips like this don't happen every day.

70
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,579
Your family can wait this one time.

71
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:09,130
Yeah.

72
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:10,738
Yeah, you're right.

73
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:12,450
I'll...

74
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:17,137
Thank you to whatever gods in
Kyoto for all the smoking areas.

75
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:18,897
Pretty sure the gods didn't do this.

76
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:22,333
Oh, by the way, I didn't forget
that 10 bucks I lent you.

77
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:23,701
Chainsmoker cat!

78
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:27,460
All right!

79
00:04:27,860 --> 00:04:29,100
Kyoto rent-room time!

80
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,520
Why Kyoto out of the blue?

81
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:35,257
Research for my manga series.

82
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:37,637
I pulled some all-nighters
to finish my deadlines.

83
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:39,249
All right, y 'all, get in!

84
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:44,077
A Kyoto adventure has
always been on my list.

85
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:47,160
Oh, and to celebrate, I
got myself a brand new car!

86
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:48,450
Whoa!

87
00:04:48,533 --> 00:04:49,920
You're making buy a new car money?

88
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:53,017
I've been getting some great
royalties from all my manga sales.

89
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:54,880
Also, this is a research trip.

90
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:58,277
The company's gonna cover everything
so we can do whatever we want!

91
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,197
Are you serious?

92
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,110
Are you serious?

93
00:05:00,193 --> 00:05:01,537
Bring me the booze.

94
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:03,326
I wanna try Kyoto cigarettes.

95
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:04,837
Are you sure about all this?

96
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,273
Sounds like write-offs!

97
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:09,478
Just remember to get receipts, okay?

98
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:16,270
Kyoto!

99
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:17,560
We are in you!

100
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:19,000
That's crazy!

101
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:20,260
The sky's so big!

102
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:23,914
The city has height restrictions
to protect the scenery.

103
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:28,180
I'm hungry after that drive.

104
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:31,017
I want to eat something
you can only get in Kyoto!

105
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:31,930
Let's go!

106
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,960
Beef falls for real?

107
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,868
Uh, you were the one
who brought us in here.

108
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:41,060
Is being cheap in my blood? That's it!

109
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:43,137
From now on, let's tear this city up!

110
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:45,044
And we'll charge it to my work!

111
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:48,820
We travel only by catch-off!

112
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:50,440
Luxury for the win!

113
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:53,545
Are you sure your company's
gonna pay for this?

114
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:55,900
It's fortune time!

115
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:58,887
You guys just get all
the ambulance you want!

116
00:05:59,020 --> 00:06:00,160
Yay, good fortune.

117
00:06:00,460 --> 00:06:01,640
Come on, good luck.

118
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:03,120
Mine's the best one.

119
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:05,800
Alright, and what's my fortune?

120
00:06:14,820 --> 00:06:18,437
The legend says, if you hate the results,
keep pulling until you get some good luck!

121
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:20,755
Sorta defeats the purpose, doesn't it?

122
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:23,120
Let's go full tilt boogie, baby.

123
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:29,817
I can see why this place is famous.

124
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:31,420
Holy shit, we're up high!

125
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:33,760
This is so strange.

126
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:37,759
Shouldn't I be having the
time of my life right now?

127
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,260
But why?

128
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:42,557
I feel like I'm being summoned.

129
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:45,020
Hatsuru, what are you doing, you dummy?

130
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,390
Huh?

131
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,473
What's gotten into you?

132
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:52,117
Did your job really give you
a blank check for this trip?

133
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,440
What? Oh, no.

134
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:57,151
No, the company's really going
to cover it, so don't worry.

135
00:06:58,860 --> 00:06:59,690
Yum!

136
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:01,720
Duck hot pot! Yay!

137
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:04,540
You're so damn good, so fucking good.

138
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:10,357
I've never had hot pot before.

139
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:13,028
Tatsuro was really
letting loose, isn't she?

140
00:07:13,620 --> 00:07:17,267
She wasn't joking when she said
she was stressed out, I guess.

141
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:22,193
It's been a while since I've
seen her have this much fun.

142
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:23,779
She'll be alright.

143
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:24,930
Don't forget,

144
00:07:25,013 --> 00:07:26,577
tomorrow we're doing
the pitch black tunnel

145
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:29,072
tour where we can't see or hear anything!

146
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:34,920
What is it?

147
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:37,454
Are we gonna get murdered or something?

148
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:39,860
Sounds great!

149
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:57,305
I almost forgot what peace and quiet felt
like with all that beast folk riffraff.

150
00:07:57,780 --> 00:08:00,180
This bottle might be too toasty, huh?

151
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:03,600
Aruneko, she's not around.

152
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:08,008
I wouldn't be surprised if
they're all out getting shitfaced.

153
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:13,057
This video was captured by the streamers
When they visited the abandoned building

154
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:17,537
This is freaky They say that a murder
happened in this room 20 years ago Really?

155
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:20,340
Oh, that's scary Come on, you're on video,

156
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:22,137
so hurry up Can't believe I found a spooky

157
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:24,926
show on TV Kind of rare
these days What is it?

158
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:30,457
It's an altar Out of unstoppable
curiosity One of the streamers

159
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:34,187
approaches the Buddhist altar
in the corner And at that moment

160
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,327
There's something behind you

161
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:40,618
It's 2026, and this is where
our special effects are?

162
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:41,897
Look at these actors.

163
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:45,980
They've got to act the hell out of
this with these so-called ghosts.

164
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:51,220
Who the hell is out there?

165
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:53,224
There shouldn't be anyone here.

166
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:54,620
That was scary.

167
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:59,020
Well, anyway, whose apartment
should I house-sit tonight?

168
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,040
Maybe I'm seeing things.

169
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:04,593
Must be all that sucky.

170
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:10,156
I guess having that Beast Folk
riff-raff around isn't so bad after all.

171
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,520
Where are you guys?

172
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,240
Come home anytime now.

173
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:38,234
It's your turn, Yanni.

174
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:39,850
Yeah.

175
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:46,260
This pitch black temple hall
is known as the Anus Tour.

176
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:50,657
There was an era where the Beast
Folk population was in steep decline.

177
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:52,657
So the Cat Buddha declared that Beast Folk

178
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:55,117
be born through both the
Birth Canal and Anus.

179
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:57,318
This sacred hall honors that legend.

180
00:09:58,060 --> 00:10:01,777
Once you've penetrated its deepest depths,
you'll find the Beast Folk's stone.

181
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:04,277
Receive its blessing by
touching it before leaving.

182
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:05,190
Wow!

183
00:10:05,273 --> 00:10:06,717
Is there something I'm not getting?

184
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:07,797
It doesn't matter.

185
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:08,710
Let's go in.

186
00:10:08,793 --> 00:10:10,344
If it costs money, let's do it.

187
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:12,116
Six tickets, please.

188
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:13,102
With a receipt.

189
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:14,557
I knew something was up.

190
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:16,037
You're acting strange again.

191
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,777
Hey, hold on. Wait for us.

192
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:19,272
Please enjoy your visit.

193
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:24,407
This temple corridor is the anus
tour, blah, blah, blah, blah.

194
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:25,370
Whoa.

195
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:26,677
This looks weird.

196
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:27,590
Let's check it out.

197
00:10:27,673 --> 00:10:28,503
Oh, okay.

198
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,877
Dark places really get your heart racing.

199
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:36,317
He wasn't kidding when
he said pitch black.

200
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:39,720
I really can't see anything
at all. You're right.

201
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:43,027
I know, we can guide
ourselves with the wall.

202
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,110
Wanna hold hands?

203
00:10:44,193 --> 00:10:45,023
I'll be okay.

204
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:50,297
Seems like Imoko really likes living
on the edge with things like this.

205
00:10:50,380 --> 00:10:53,321
Is it just me, or is it
starting to stink in here?

206
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:57,000
Yeah, it smells like cigarettes.

207
00:10:57,500 --> 00:11:00,857
I can't believe someone would
actually smoke in a place like this.

208
00:11:00,940 --> 00:11:02,897
Oh my god, there are
butts all over the ground.

209
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:04,217
I just stepped on some!

210
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,130
Ew!

211
00:11:05,213 --> 00:11:06,240
Oh, look up ahead!

212
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:08,200
It's getting brighter!

213
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:10,237
Yeah, you're right, it is!

214
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:11,150
Hurry up!

215
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,470
Oh!

216
00:11:14,553 --> 00:11:15,420
Whoa, look, Yomuko!

217
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:18,380
It's the Beast Folk Stone!

218
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:22,780
The sacred Beast Folk Stone is
believed to have created Beast Folk.

219
00:11:22,920 --> 00:11:24,160
In times of crisis,

220
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:27,917
it served as the Cat Buddha's vessel
and would talk down to its people.

221
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,040
I can sense the spiritual power.

222
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:32,417
Hmm, could I use this for inspiration?

223
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:36,280
It's like I can feel the
weight of history. What is it?

224
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:39,777
Someone's been putting out their
butts on this sacred stone!

225
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:41,272
Look, that's disgusting!

226
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:43,077
How inconsiderate can you be?

227
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:46,197
And I bet the criminal was trying
to hide their desecration, too.

228
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:48,537
You can tell whoever did this
was nothing but a failure

229
00:11:48,620 --> 00:11:51,502
about how they couldn't
even clean up their mess.

230
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:52,810
Crazy.

231
00:11:52,893 --> 00:11:55,377
The whole way out was
littered with butts, too!

232
00:11:55,460 --> 00:11:57,519
This sacred temple tour was ruined!

233
00:11:57,960 --> 00:12:00,637
Well, I don't see any
signs saying no smoking.

234
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,337
Yeah, but you shouldn't litter.

235
00:12:02,420 --> 00:12:05,302
Makes you wonder what kind
of parent raised them.

236
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,230
That's weird.

237
00:12:10,313 --> 00:12:12,637
It sure did sound like little
sis's voice for a minute.

238
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:13,550
Come on, Yanni.

239
00:12:13,633 --> 00:12:15,597
I think I saw a trash can
we can ditch these butts in.

240
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:17,137
I got rid of them already.

241
00:12:17,220 --> 00:12:18,050
What?

242
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:25,480
Being able to smoke at
home is the absolute best!

243
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,537
Miju Castle is the ancient location where

244
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:32,760
Tokugawa Yoshinobu
declared the Nyansei Hokan.

245
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:36,017
The castle tour shows
you aspects of beast folk

246
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:38,117
history that they don't
teach you in school.

247
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:39,217
I have a question.

248
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,594
What's the Nyansei Hokan you mentioned?

249
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:45,077
It was a declaration made by
the Tokugawa Shogunate that

250
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:48,454
gave ownership of beast folk
to the imperial government.

251
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:51,346
Alright, let's head
inside and start the tour.

252
00:12:51,780 --> 00:12:55,217
The art of Nyado was very
popular during the Edo Shogunate.

253
00:12:55,300 --> 00:12:59,637
This exhibition displays a variety of
items belonging to a late Nyado master,

254
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:01,480
Furuta Nyasuke. Nyado?

255
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:05,409
Humans and beast folk have been
on good terms for centuries.

256
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:07,100
During this era,

257
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:11,640
the beast folk would dress in unique
